   "displayId": "textTurn_exploreDataFromNL_1792307048893_closing",
   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**South Sudan has the lowest estimated high school completion rate among countries with data: just 2% in 2025.** The lowest rates are concentrated in sub-Saharan Africa.\n\nThe five lowest are:\n- **South Sudan:** 2.1%\n- **Niger:** 4.9%\n- **Central African Republic:** 5.6%\n- **Chad:** 6.6%\n- **Zimbabwe:** 8.1%\n\nHere, “high school” means upper secondary education. The map uses each country’s latest estimate from 2020–2025—all available values were for 2025—and combines girls and boys. Some countries lack estimates; territories with fewer than 100,000 people are excluded.\n\nSource: UIS, February 2026 release.",
   "parentNodeId": "d_out_3",
